'''CAG Osaka''', formerly known as '''CYCLOPS athlete gaming''' and '''Cyclops Osaka''', is a [[:Category:Japan|Japanese]] esports organization.<br>On July 1st, 2026, '''CAG''' announced their team integration with '''[[VARREL]]'''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/CYCLOPS_OSAKA/status/2072206070966349948|title=VARRELとのチーム統合のお知らせ|trans_title=Announcement: Team Integration with VARREL|author='''CAG OSAKA'''|language={{flag|jp}} Japanese|date=2026-07-01}}</ref>

==Timeline==
{{tabs dynamic
|name1=2016
|name2=2017
|name3=2022
|name4=2023
|name5=2024
|name6=2025
|name7=2026
|This=7
|content1=
* November 13th - The Fighting Game division is created, consisting of [[GO1]], [[Tanukana]], and [[Dogura]].
|content2=
* October 26th - A merger with ''INFINITY OSAKA'' is announced for December 1st, 2017.<ref name="CYCLOPS athlete gaming will merge with INFINITY OSAKA">{{cite web |url=https://www.daily.co.jp/general/2017/10/26/0010674734.shtml |title=CYCLOPS athlete gaming will merge with INFINITY OSAKA. |date=2017-10-26 |language={{Flag|jp}} Japanese |publisher= [https://www.daily.co.jp Daily Sports]}}</ref>
* December 1st - [[Fenritti]] joins the roster.<ref name="Fenritti joins">{{cite web|url=http://cyclops-osaka.jp/2017/12/01/3927/|title=新メンバー加入のお知らせ|publisher=[[CYCLOPS athlete gaming]]|date=2017-12-01}}</ref>
|content3=
* February 17th - [[Tanukana]] is released.<ref name="Tanukana released">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/CYCLOPS_OSAKA/status/1494146366699753475|title=たぬかな|publisher=[[CYCLOPS athlete gaming]]|date=2022-02-17}}</ref>
|content4=
* April 6th - [[Dogura]] leaves.<ref name="Dogura leaves">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/CYCLOPS_OSAKA/status/1643939811328421888|title=先ほど定例配信内でお伝えした通り|publisher=[[CYCLOPS athlete gaming]]|date=2023-04-06}}</ref>
* May 10th - CYCLOPS athlete gaming announces their [[Street Fighter League/Japan/2023|Street Fighter League Pro-JP 2023]] roster, consisting of [[GO1]], [[Fenritti]], [[Kazunoko]] and [[Dogura]].<ref name="SFL Pro-JP 2023 announcement">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/CAPCOM_eSports/status/1656479806249373700|date=2023-05-10|title=ストリートファイターリーグ: Pro-JP 2023 1stステージ 出場選手発表|publisher=[https://twitter.com/CAPCOM_eSports Capcom Esports]|language={{Flag|jp}} Japanese}}</ref>
* June 1st - [[Eita]] joins the roster.<ref name="CAG Eita">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/CYCLOPS_OSAKA/status/1664225289906573314|title=格闘ゲーム部門 選手加入のお知らせ|publisher=[[CYCLOPS athlete gaming]]|date=2023-06-01}}</ref>
|content5=
* May 25th - [[Uryo]] joins.<ref name="CAG Uryo">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/CYCLOPS_OSAKA/status/1794217426294591725|title=格闘ゲーム部門 選手加入: この度、うりょ選手(@uryoryon )が CAG OSAKAへ加入しました。|publisher=[[CYCLOPS athlete gaming]]|date=2024-05-25}}</ref>
* May 25th - CYCLOPS athlete gaming announces their [[Street Fighter League/Japan/2024|Street Fighter League Pro-JP 2024]] roster, consisting of [[GO1]], [[Fenritti]], [[Eita]] and [[Uryo]].<ref name="SFL Pro-JP 2024 announcement">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/CAPCOM_eSports/status/1656479806249373700|date=2024-05-25|title=◤◢◤SFL2024 　CAG OSAKA◢◤◢第4の選手|publisher=[[CYCLOPS athlete gaming]]|language={{Flag|jp}} Japanese}}</ref>
|content6=
* March 31st - [[GO1]] leaves.<ref name="GO1 leaves">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/CYCLOPS_OSAKA/status/1906632561729875970|title=このたび、格闘ゲーム部門のGO1(@GO13151)選手が契約期間満了に伴い、退団することとなりました。|publisher=[[CYCLOPS athlete gaming]]|date=2025-03-31}}</ref>
* June 7th - CAG Osaka's [[Street Fighter League/Japan/2025|Street Fighter League Pro-JP 2025]] roster is announced, consisting of [[Fenritti]], [[Eita]], [[Uryo]] and [[Takagi]].<ref name="SFL Pro-JP 2025 announcement">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/CYCLOPS_OSAKA/status/1931275476695142764|date=2024-06-07|title=【高木選手 SFL参戦】|publisher=Twitter |author=CAG Osaka|language={{Flag|jp}} Japanese}}</ref> 
* November 14th - CAG Osaka signs [[Kido]] to their Academy roster.<ref name="Kido joins">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/CYCLOPS_OSAKA/status/1989241904194543637|title=格闘ゲームアカデミー 始動|publisher=Twitter |author=[[CAG Osaka]]|language={{Flag|jp}} Japanese|date=2025-11-14}}</ref> 
|content7=
* March 4th - CAG Osaka announces they will not compete in the [[Street Fighter League/Japan/2026|Street Fighter League Pro-JP 2026]] season.<ref name="CAG Osaka departured SFL Pro-JP 2026">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/CYCLOPS_OSAKA/status/2029104563752714274|title=【SFL 2026シーズン参加辞退および格闘ゲーム部門活動休止のお知らせ】|publisher=X |author=[[CAG Osaka]]|language={{Flag|jp}} Japanese|date=2026-03-04}}</ref> 
* March 31st - CAG Osaka disbands their fighting game roster. [[Fenritti]], [[Eita]] and [[Uryo]] all leave the team.<ref name="CAG Osaka disbanded Fighting games division">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/CYCLOPS_OSAKA/status/2038979350079640006|title=先般ご報告の通り、格闘ゲーム部門は2026年3月末をもって活動を休止いたします。|publisher=X |author=[[CAG Osaka]]|language={{Flag|jp}} Japanese|date=2025-03-31}}</ref>
}}

